@tradition name-on-the-beam
// Name on the beam (0.60.7, the traditions engineer, plans/plan-0607.html "Traditions"): after your first full shift
// the Works crew gather under the Works bay's cross beam and you paint your name beside everyone who's served there.
// Zeke hands you the pen. Your first Monday (day 1), straight from shift: the crew come as they clock off (after-shift).
// The beam and your name on it are the deck architect's (trace nameOnBeam, a lasting mark from the day you join).
k: 441
title: Name on the beam
when: arrival monday
at: 17:05-18:00
min: 15
prio: 2
after-shift: yes
venue: works-bay
where: 5 room Works bay: work:works, free
where: 5 room Tea corner: lounge-seat
hold: none
who: calder always, torres-zeke always, pell 95%, works 80%
anim: talk
host: calder
from: calder
trace: nameOnBeam

== mail
- After your shift tomorrow, stay in the Works bay a few minutes. Every new hand signs the beam. Bring nothing; Zeke has the pen.

== ask
- Don't rush off after shift. There's a beam with a gap on it, just your size.   #funny
- After shift, under the cross beam. Every new hand signs it.
- Zeke's got the pen ready. He's been practising handing it over.   #funny

== here
- Every name up there did a first shift, same as you.   #warm
- Big letters. Nobody can read the small ones.   #funny
- Mine's the faded one by the bolt. Ten years, near enough.   #warm

== thanks
- Zeke hands you the pen. You paint your name on the cross beam, beside everyone who's served in the Works. The crew clap.   #warm

== chatter
- Did you see the new name on the beam? Still wet.
- The beam's nearly full on the port side. We'll start the starboard soon.   #funny
- I read the beam sometimes. Every name's a story.   #warm
